<title>TAIWAN: Taiwan CK Group buys 54,000T U.S. corn at tender.</title>
<headline>Taiwan CK Group buys 54,000T U.S. corn at tender.</headline>
<dateline>TAIPEI 1997-01-30</dateline>
<text>
<p>Taiwan's CK group bought a 54,000-tonne shipment of U.S. No.2 corn from Agrex at a tender on Thursday, traders said.</p>
<p>The CK Group comprises Chia Hsin Flour Feed and Vegetable Oil Corp and some buyers from Taiwan's southern port city of Kaohsiung.  </p>
<p>The shipment was bought on a cost-and-freight basis, traders said.</p>
<p>Details for the tender are as follows:</p>
<p>	    U.S. Gulf	     Pacific N.W.</p>
<p> 27,500   March 20-April 4    April 5-19    US$143.30</p>
<p> 26,500   March 20-April 4    April 5-19    91.33 US cents/May</p>
<p>--Taipei Newsroom (2-5080815)</p>
